  "tuning_disclosure": {
    "rusteda": "The RustEDA arm is the producer behind the published GF180MCU D row: aligned selects with the area goal, hold and measured-load repair, and Metal2/top-metal floating fill, developed over the recorded GF180 trials against the shared gates' power, area, Fmax and density findings, not against LibreLane's runtime.",
    "librelane": "Every LibreLane arm runs the same floating-fill emitter as RustEDA on its own final GDS, with the same options, so both flows are judged on density with fill. The emitter cannot lift LibreLane's top metal to its 30 % geometric target (26.0 % on the published layout); it emits what fits and the foundry density rules decide. The published configuration uses LibreLane's defaults for antenna repair and post-GRT resizer margins; this plan screens it against the IHP recipe's closure settings and jumper-only antenna repair, the knob classes of the IHP screen. Fill is GDS geometry only: OpenRCX, the timing gate and the power figures do not see it.",
    "harness": "LibreLane runs with TMPDIR=/tmp (tmpfs), where the published SKY130A and GF180MCU D runs kept Yosys's ABC temporary files. With TMPDIR on the ext4 /home volume, Yosys 0.70's parallel ABC mapping hung in synthesis in 3 of 3 runs (2026-11-17); with /tmp it finished in 92 s with the published synthesis netlist. Yosys also writes a merged-Liberty cache there under a new key in every run (as in the published run), so no sample reuses another's."
  },
